sequenceDiagram
    actor User as User (Web or Slack)
    participant Transport as Web/Slack transport
    participant Bot as Bot core
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant GH as GitHub App/API
    participant Daytona as Daytona sandbox
    participant Claude as Claude Code
    participant S3 as S3 artifact slots

    User->>Transport: Send request
    Transport->>DB: Load org config / principal
    Transport->>Bot: HandleRequest(org, text, thread, user, options, agent, model)

    Bot->>DB: Create durable agent_run and claim active thread slot
    Bot->>DB: Load conversation, saved task options, model, agent slug

    alt No conversation and no default repo
        Bot-->>Transport: Notify "Which repository?"
        Bot->>DB: Save partial conversation (history[0], agent/model/options)
        Bot->>DB: Mark agent_run succeeded
        Transport-->>User: Ask for owner/name
    else Repo selected or default repo exists
        Bot->>DB: Resolve agent profile and task options
        Bot->>GH: Look up cached repo and mint repo-scoped installation token
        GH-->>Bot: owner/repo, base branch, short-lived token

        Bot-->>User: Starting / sandbox status block
        Bot->>Daytona: Create sandbox from snapshot with labels/cache volume
        Daytona-->>Bot: Sandbox ID
        Bot->>DB: Upsert conversation with repo, sandbox_id, branch

        alt Validate changes is enabled
            Bot->>DB: Get repo_setup_spec
            alt Spec not found
                Bot->>Daytona: Bootstrap session: clone, detect hints, run bootstrap loop
                Daytona->>Claude: Opus/high bootstrap prompt
                Claude-->>Daytona: manifest.json, setup.sh, start.sh, health.sh
                Bot->>DB: Save validated/partial spec or failing partial spec
            else Spec exists
                Bot->>Bot: Reuse saved spec as-is
            end
            Bot->>S3: Mint proof artifact upload slots (if configured)
        end

        Bot->>Daytona: Write and run agent.sh or followup.sh
        loop Agent output
            Daytona-->>Bot: Hetchy-framed stdout/stderr lines
            Bot->>DB: Append agent_run_events
            Bot-->>Transport: Fan out block_start/append/done
            Transport-->>User: SSE blocks or Slack thread updates
        end

        Claude->>GH: Push branch and create/update pull request
        Claude-->>Daytona: Final text contains PR URL
        Daytona-->>Bot: Command completed
        Bot->>GH: Verify PR URL, repo, head branch, base branch when fresh
        GH-->>Bot: Verified PR
        Bot->>DB: Persist conversation turn and response_blocks
        Bot->>DB: Mark agent_run succeeded
        Bot->>Daytona: Delete session, stop sandbox, archive sandbox
        Bot-->>Transport: Done block with PR URL
        Transport-->>User: Final result
    end

    Note over Bot,DB: For follow-ups, the existing conversation has sandbox_id + pr_url. Hetchy starts the archived sandbox, mints a fresh GitHub token, runs followup.sh on the same branch, appends a new turn, then archives again on success.
